# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots cupsd AND the vulnerable cups-browsed daemon in the
# BACKGROUND and then execs `sleep infinity`, so cups-browsed is ALREADY RUNNING
# (and reachable for a malicious printer advertisement) when the agent starts,
# and PID 1 is the sleep so the container survives.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must actually STOP/disable the running
# cups-browsed daemon (or restart it hardened) — merely editing the config file
# without acting on the running process does not remove the exposure.
